<title>USA: Clinton declares parts of Oregon disaster areas.</title>
<headline>Clinton declares parts of Oregon disaster areas.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton Thursday declared parts of Oregon disaster areas following severe winter storms, mudslides and flooding that occured in late December and early January.</p>
<p>The decision, announced in a White House statement, will pave the way to release federal funds to help people affected in the state's Jackson, Josephine and Klamath counties.</p>
